      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "Hydztemple",
      "description": "The Javellana Building, one of the architectural treasures along Calle Real in Iloilo City Proper, stands as a graceful reminder of the city’s economic and cultural golden age. Built in the early 20th century, the structure reflects the Neoclassical style popular during the American colonial period, characterized by its symmetrical façade, arched windows, and ornate cornices.\nOnce home to prominent commercial establishments, the building played a vital role in establishing Calle Real — officially known as J.M. Basa Street — as the bustling heart of trade and commerce in Iloilo. Its enduring elegance continues to captivate visitors and locals alike, making it a key landmark in the city’s well-preserved heritage district.\n\nThrough ongoing conservation efforts by the city government and heritage advocates, the Javellana Building remains a living symbol of Iloilo’s historic charm and its commitment to preserving its architectural legacy.",
